Package: enum2x2
Type: Package
Title: Every 2x2 Table Compatible with a Published Agreement Statistic
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Elliot", "Tower", email = "elliot@elliottower.ai",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7004-8884"))
Description: A study comparing two binary criteria on one population computes
    its numbers from a 2x2 table, then publishes the numbers and not the table.
    Given a sample size, both positive marginals and Cohen's kappa as the
    strings a source printed, this package enumerates every non-negative
    integer table whose statistics round back to those digits. Rounding is
    treated as a constraint rather than as noise: a printed figure names a
    closed interval, and membership is decided by integer cross-multiplication,
    so there is no tolerance parameter. The result is reported as uniquely
    identified, set-identified with the span of each cell, infeasible, or
    insufficiently reported. The interface mirrors 'metafor::conv.2x2()', which
    reconstructs one table per row by optimization, so the two can be compared
    directly.
